<%#
Cistergraphia: Inscribe (fol. 1r)
=================================

Purpose:
- Write a message as a Cistergraphia, in game or secret mode
- Teach how a sign is read, beside the form

Design Decisions:
- Mode is an explicit choice (two index cards, red and blue) rather than an
  optional field; the passphrase only appears for the secret (JS), and is
  always present, labelled, without JS
- The key (anatomy, tabula, order) is drawn from the real cipher geometry; the
  anatomy's corners are dials (JS enables them; static without JS)
- The live preview draws each letter's sign from the same geometry (JSON from
  ViewHelpers#glyph_table_json); the plate itself is only made on the server
- Layout (reading path) is a second, quieter choice: Phaistos (the snail) by
  default, or Rongorongo; the key's "Order of reading" follows it (JS; both
  are shown without JS). The decoder detects the layout, so it is never asked

Constraints:
- Posts to /generate; message limited to 500 characters
%>
<div class="spread">
  <section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="inscribe-title">
    <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 1<sup>r</sup></p>
    <h1 id="inscribe-title" class="rubric">Inscribe a message</h1>
    <p class="lede">Each letter becomes a number, each number a monk’s sign, and the signs coil inward like a snail, or turn like a tablet.</p>

    <form class="entry" method="post" action="/generate" data-entry>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="message">Message</label>
        <textarea id="message" name="message" maxlength="500" rows="4" required
                  placeholder="Meet me at the old abbey after vespers" data-counted></textarea>
        <p class="field-meta">
          <span data-mode-note="game">Letters and spaces only; anything else becomes a space.</span>
          <span data-mode-note="secret" hidden>Any text: capitals, digits, accents, emoji.</span>
          <span class="counter" data-counter aria-live="polite"><span data-count>0</span> / 500</span>
        </p>
        <div class="preview" data-preview data-glyph-table="<%= glyph_table_json %>" hidden>
          <p class="preview-label">
            <span class="label">Preview</span>
            <span class="preview-hint" data-mode-note="game">each letter as one sign, before it is split in two and coiled</span>
            <span class="preview-hint" data-mode-note="secret" hidden>sealed messages have no preview: their signs come from the encryption</span>
          </p>
          <ol class="preview-signs" data-preview-signs aria-hidden="true"></ol>
          <p class="preview-empty" data-preview-empty>Start typing to see your letters as signs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="modes">
        <legend>Mode</legend>
        <div class="mode-options">
          <label class="mode mode--game">
            <input type="radio" name="mode" value="game" checked>
            <span class="mode-title">Game</span>
            <span class="mode-desc">A puzzle in the old manner. Patient readers, and machines, can solve it.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="mode mode--secret">
            <input type="radio" name="mode" value="secret">
            <span class="mode-title">Secret</span>
            <span class="mode-desc">Sealed with a passphrase (AES-256-GCM). The image shows only its length.</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset class="modes layouts">
        <legend>Layout <span class="label-note">· the order of reading</span></legend>
        <div class="mode-options">
          <label class="mode mode--path">
            <input type="radio" name="layout" value="phaistos" checked>
            <span class="mode-title">Phaistos</span>
            <span class="mode-desc">The snail: clockwise from the top-left corner, coiling to the centre.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="mode mode--path">
            <input type="radio" name="layout" value="rongorongo">
            <span class="mode-title">Rongorongo</span>
            <span class="mode-desc">From the bottom up, turning the plate half round at every line.</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="field" data-secret-only>
        <label for="passphrase">Passphrase <span class="label-note">· secret mode only</span></label>
        <div class="passphrase">
          <input type="password" id="passphrase" name="passphrase" minlength="8"
                 autocomplete="new-password" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-reveal="passphrase" aria-pressed="false">Show</button>
        </div>
        <p class="field-meta"><span>At least 8 characters; four or more random words is far better. Never stored.</span></p>
      </div>

      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit" data-submit>Inscribe</button>
    </form>
  </section>

  <aside class="leaf" aria-labelledby="key-title">
    <h2 id="key-title" class="rubric rubric--small">How to read a sign</h2>

    <figure class="anatomy" data-anatomy data-number="1098">
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--tens" data-place="10" disabled><b data-digit>9</b>tens</button>
      <%== glyph_svg(1098, title: '1098: one thousand, no hundreds, nine tens, eight units') %>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--units" data-place="1" disabled><b data-digit>8</b>units</button>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--thousands" data-place="1000" disabled><b data-digit>1</b>thousands</button>
      <button type="button" class="quadrant quadrant--hundreds" data-place="100" disabled><b data-digit>0</b>hundreds</button>
      <figcaption>One stem, four corners: <span data-anatomy-caption>1098, the founding of Cîteaux</span>.</figcaption>
      <p class="anatomy-hint" data-anatomy-hint hidden>Touch a corner to turn its digit.</p>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="index-heading">Tabula of units</h3>
    <ol class="tabula">
      <% (1..9).each do |digit| %>
        <li><%== glyph_svg(digit) %><span aria-hidden="true"><%= digit %></span></li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Tens mirror the units to the left, hundreds below, thousands both ways.</p>

    <h3 class="index-heading">Order of reading</h3>
    <figure class="order" data-layout-note="phaistos">
      <%== snail_svg(4) %>
      <figcaption><b>Phaistos.</b> Clockwise from the top-left corner, coiling to the centre.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="order" data-layout-note="rongorongo">
      <%== snail_svg(4, layout: :rongorongo) %>
      <figcaption><b>Rongorongo.</b> From the bottom left, then turn the plate half round for each next line.
        Hollow points are signs written upside down.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="note"><a href="/about#why-a-snail">Why these two?</a></p>
  </aside>
</div>
